statement:
`security[i]` is the number of guards on duty on day `i` (days are numbered from `0`), and `time` is a non-negative integer. Day `i` counts as a good day exactly when all of these hold:

- at least `time` days come before day `i` and at least `time` days come after it;
- over the window from day `i - time` to day `i`, the guard count never goes up: `security[i - time] >= ... >= security[i]`;
- over the window from day `i` to day `i + time`, the guard count never goes down: `security[i] <= ... <= security[i + time]`.

Return all good days, in any order.

validator:
function validate([security, time]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(security) || security.length < 1 || security.length > 100000) return 'security needs 1 to 100000 days.';
  if (security.some(v => !Number.isInteger(v) || v < 0 || v > 100000)) return 'Each guard count is an integer from 0 to 100000.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(time) || time < 0 || time > 100000) return 'time is an integer from 0 to 100000.';
  return null;
}

